<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Strandbeests

Wind-walking kinetic creatures of Elyncia's Gaia-bleed coastlines: descendants of Theo Jansen's
sculptures given improbable life, striding the tide-flats on articulated legs, powered by weather.
They graze the shore the way herds graze grass — on wind, on salt, on whatever the water leaves.

''They live where the Datum put the water.'' The strandbeest belt runs the shore-climate the
''Apophis Datum'' installed in YOLD 3195 — the ~10m re-basing that fixed every coastline most of
Elyncia now calls ordinary. The whole lineage and the symbiotic life riding it occupy a habitat
that exists ''because a goddess caught her sister's asteroid''. Nobody walking the flats thinks
about it. The beests simply live at the water level mercy left behind.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/domestication>>

!! Self-Domestication ~ the mycelial bond

''Some strandbeests — never all — domesticated themselves.'' They did it by symbiosing with the
''Mycelial-Mother-Cultures'' of the Fungus Folk: a fungal intelligence takes root in the frame,
and the beest that carries one comes in off the flats and stays.

''Nobody tamed them.'' No halter, no breaking, no bargain struck with a herder. The bond forms
between beest and culture, and tameness arrives as a ''consequence'' of that bond rather than as
its purpose. A wild beest and a domesticated one differ by what lives in the struts.

''What the pairing does.'' A bonded beest serves as a ''mobile ephyra and troop-homunculi
platform'' — the culture raises tasked spirits and mushroom-ashigaru aboard a frame that walks
them wherever the Circles need them. Fungal logistics on legs. The Fungus Folk build no supply
train because the supply train grows its own cargo and carries itself.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-great-beests>>

!! The Great Beests ~ walking reefs

''The truly large ones carry full Mother-Cultures'' — not a rooted fragment but a whole distributed
intelligence — alongside the rest of their ''Datum-shore symbiotic life''. Barnacle-analogues,
salt-flora, spore-lichens, nesting things, and whatever else has found a purchase across decades of
striding.

''They read as walking dry-coral reefs.'' Reef-life over every strut, a slow ecology moving at
walking pace across the flats, hosting more species than the ground it crosses. A great beest is
less an animal than ''a place that travels''.

''Scale runs the whole ladder.'' Juveniles pull carts. Mature beests carry rooted culture-fragments
and a working crew of ephyra. The great ones carry nations of small life and a Mother-Culture that
answers as itself. What a frame can host scales with what a frame can bear.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-anomaly>>

!! The Anomaly ~ what happened in Aki's clearing

Against all of the above, ''the Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine reads wrong on two counts'':

# ''A full Mother Culture on a juvenile frame.'' Full cultures ride the great beests. This one rides
  a small tame beest of burden.
# ''A Mother Culture AND a Lararium on the same frame.'' The mycelial bond has only ever run as a
  ''pair''. A Lares node joined it — a third party walking into a symbiosis with no room in it —
  and nothing in the Fungus Folk's long practice accounts for that.

''The Circles hold opinions.'' Whether the shrine reads as a new kind of thing, a violation, an
opportunity, or a claim to be collected stands open — and the priesthood whose anchored Mother
Spore dispatched the Ephyra in the first place has never had its tasked spirit returned.

Full event: [[strandbeest-shrine|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/companions/strandbeest-shrine]].

<<~/ahu>>

